  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan\rFXL-002 P1\rFXL-003 P1\rFXL-004 P1\rFXL-005 P1\rFXL-012 P3\rFXL-013 P3\rFXL-014 P3\rFXL-015 P3\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The glazing serving the upper flank elevation of the development indicated on drawing Nos. FXL-013 P3 and FXL-015 P3; shall be fixed shut 1.7m above floor level and in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 5 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved drawings, and prior to above ground works, detailed drawings of the proposed side window and its surrounding detailing shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall be provided at a scale of between 1:1 and 1:20 and shall include elevations and sections of the proposed window, together with details of the window frame, materials, colour, finish, glazing arrangement, reveal depths, cills, lintels, and the treatment of the surrounding brickwork. Details of any new bricks, including their specification, bonding pattern, colour, texture, and pointing, shall also be provided. The development shall thereafter be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance within the Lakes Conservation Area.\r"
  ],
